{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod","id":1414694,"title":"Famous in the WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-19T22:40:47-07:00","id":1414694,"title":"Famous in the WoD","content":"I had one of those proverbial refrigerator moments today \u2013 doing something unrelated and then had a random WoD idea pop into my head.<br /> <br /> What if some of the NPCs of VtM were famous as mortals in the WoD?<br /> <br /> What if Horatio Ballard is known and ranked alongside George Westinghouse and John D Rockefeller? What is Lucita is a much romanticized Lost Princess? What if Theo Bell is known as a folk hero from around the American Civil War?<br /> <br /> So maybe John Goodman played a fictional Ballard in a supporting role in some 1990s movie. Maybe legends about the \u201cGhost of Lucita haunting Zaragoza\u201d have been the inspiration for several movies and TV programs. Maybe rappers drop the name Theo Bell into lyrics sometimes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T03:49:58-07:00","id":1414710,"title":"","content":"I imagine a lot of the princes are famous. Vampires travel to different cities and have to present themselves to them. If the princes are worth their salt, they will be remembered. I would guess everybody knew the eternal prince of london.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 09-20-2020, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T03:57:36-07:00","id":1414711,"title":"","content":"well, people seem religiously opposed to recognize vampires as being mythological gods so...yeah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T05:21:33-07:00","id":1414714,"title":"","content":"In my round the TL of my Mage is a Vampire that is famous for how her &quot;husband&quot; (sire) rescued her from the Nazis during the Reichskristallnacht so yeah it could work. Though it is way better for the masquerade, if you are either famous long ago, being able to use fleshforming to change your look or able to make a famous end and then go into torpor for like a century so if someone find your body until it is just the corpse kept cool by some crazy fan and later you are just some lookalike or &quot;Elvisdressup&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T06:28:08-07:00","id":1414725,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s a great idea!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T07:12:27-07:00","id":1414729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1414725#post1414725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s a great idea!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T07:30:33-07:00","id":1414730,"title":"","content":"Must admit exploring fame pre-embrace or of past identities is not something i can remember doing, curiously.<br /> The Lucita part - and maybe someone doing a Disney movie (that i imagine, based on her lifestory and temper, as possibly being WoD's parallel equivalent of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6CKcqIahedc\" target=\"_blank\">Brave</a>) - is an image that sends me in nonstop giggling fits. Damn, i'm half-tempted to sketch a fake summary for &quot;Valente&quot; just for the trolling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-20-2020, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T07:48:44-07:00","id":1414734,"title":"","content":"Smiling Jack is often listed among notorious pirates, there's a bar named after him in Key West, and some sources cite him as an inspiration for Captain Jack Sparrow.<br /> <br /> The <b>Chicago By Night</b> characters lifted from Upton Sinclair's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Jungle\" target=\"_blank\">The Jungle</a> are semi-famous because in the setting it's a true story and perhaps has had a few more adaptations - Tamoszius resents that his role was cut down to a cameo in the HBO series in 1996.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T08:22:47-07:00","id":1414742,"title":"","content":"Victoria Ash actually was apparently a famous pop star for about a minute in the Nineties in what was something only a Toreador elder could pull off. My assumption is that she was someone who roughly paralleled Pink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T12:08:51-07:00","id":1415100,"title":"","content":"I definitely think that is the case. When I ran a chronicle in Chicago, I basically used Horatio Ballard as a replacement for Philip Danforth Armour. Armour was a meatpacking titan based out of Chicago which Ballard was as well. Armour's company was also the basis for Upton Sinclair's The Jungle, which was hugely influential inf irst edition Chicago By Night, so it was doubly appropriate. <br /> <br /> So anything Armour did, I transferred to Ballard. That meant renaming the Armour Square neighborhood in Chicago Ballard Square, and plastering Ballard's name everywhere like at the Illinois Institute of Technology (which was originally the Armour Institute, so now it was the Ballard Institute.) I then turned Ballard up to 11 and made him as historically well known as the other famous Robber Barons - Carnegie, Rockefeller, Morgan, etc.<br /> <br /> I can't remember emphasizing that with other characters, but I would again if it made sense to do so. The Fame background has always been part of the game, and even if certain vampires aren't famous now (since they've been dead for however long) sometimes they were previously famous and might still be considered historically relevant and known.<br /> <br /> I've also had certain vampires be the source of certain urban legends and the like. These were mainly Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that Theo Bell could be a folk hero of the Civil War era.<br /> <br /> And along with Craig Oxbow, I added Smiling Jack up there with notorious real life pirates (isn't he a Blackbeard analogue?).<br /> <br /> And of course some vampires are famous as being... vampires (like Dracula). Real world has vampire legends and stories, and sometimes certain vampires become &quot;known&quot; even if it is under some kind of pseudonym created by mortal folklore or fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T14:57:41-07:00","id":1415120,"title":"","content":"I actually have Kathy Glens and Damien as two musicians a lot more famous than they really know or want to be. AC/DC basically cited Baby Chorus as their big inspiration and they also have a bunch of other bands talking about them in magazines decades after they were &quot;big,&quot;<br /> <br /> This is problematic as is the fact that their music has become ubiquitous on the internet. Not just the actual songs and performances recorded secretly or from bootleg CDs but also covers. Its hard to hide, &quot;World's Greatest Guitarist&quot; and &quot;World's Greatest Drummer&quot; from your resume even if it had to have been electronically sped up.<br /> <br /> Frankly, defacing their Wikipedia page just isn't going to cut it anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T08:58:23-07:00","id":1415197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1415100#post1415100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely think that is the case. When I ran a chronicle in Chicago, I basically used Horatio Ballard as a replacement for Philip Danforth Armour. Armour was a meatpacking titan based out of Chicago which Ballard was as well. Armour's company was also the basis for Upton Sinclair's The Jungle, which was hugely influential inf irst edition Chicago By Night, so it was doubly appropriate.<br /> <br /> So anything Armour did, I transferred to Ballard. That meant renaming the Armour Square neighborhood in Chicago Ballard Square, and plastering Ballard's name everywhere like at the Illinois Institute of Technology (which was originally the Armour Institute, so now it was the Ballard Institute.) I then turned Ballard up to 11 and made him as historically well known as the other famous Robber Barons - Carnegie, Rockefeller, Morgan, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is great and exactly the kind of thing I was think of. It gives some character to the WoD, more so than just being &quot;our world with vampires.&quot; It also would give an odd quality to any vampire who knows history meeting Ballard, as he is a historical figure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1415100#post1415100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that Theo Bell could be a folk hero of the Civil War era..</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I should expand on the idea....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1415120#post1415120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually have Kathy Glens and Damien as two musicians a lot more famous than they really know or want to be. AC/DC basically cited Baby Chorus as their big inspiration....</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that a lot. But how does this work for the time line, given AC/DC started in 1973 in Australia and Baby Chorus was not really a thing until the 1980s in Chicago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T13:13:18-07:00","id":1415228,"title":"","content":"Could easily switch AC/DC for a prominent punk bad in nineties or later.<br /> <br /> Then again, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Af5Kjgs8BI4\" target=\"_blank\">the Chicago Punk scene has always been neglected nationally</a>. Local Chicago favorites like Naked Raygun are practically unknown elsewhere in the US. I'd prefer that if Baby Chorus is known, it'd be among a small musical elite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T13:43:45-07:00","id":1415235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1415197#post1415197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that a lot. But how does this work for the time line, given AC/DC started in 1973 in Australia and Baby Chorus was not really a thing until the 1980s in Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, AC/DC modified their sound and evolved in the World of Darkness but that was because I saw Baby Chorus having a harder rock than pure punk sound than a pure 90s Goth band would due to Kathy Glens influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T21:26:48-07:00","id":1415260,"title":"","content":"Fabrizio Ulfila was the Gothic bishop <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulfilas\" target=\"_blank\">Ulfilas</a> and Embraced in Constantinople by Antonius. Back in the day he was a lot more well-known than he is now.<br /> <br /> While there was a lot of pushback in Revised books against the idea of &quot;George Washington was a vampire,&quot; and rightly so (early books could be a little gonzo about it), more obscure historical figures make great vampires. I've made <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barthelemy_Lafon\" target=\"_blank\">Barth\u00e9lemy Lafon</a> rather than Jean Lafitte a vampire, Embraced by a Toreador who didn't want to lose his talents to yellow fever. Marie Laveau wasn't a vampire, but there is an elder who claims to have been Dr. John, the houngan who taught her everything she knew. He may or may not be lying.<br /> <br /> Beyond vampires, mages can make even better famous people. I recall some pretty recent Mage material having Queen Victoria be a Technocrat.<br /> <br /> And of course, with wraiths, you can go all out. I recall a thread in which a poster had Julius Caesar be the Smiling Lord, which I liked. Why not, when you have Bismarck as the anacreon of Berlin and Qin Shi Huang as the ruler of Yellow Springs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T21:32:41-07:00","id":1415262,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea of vampires being Embraced AFTER the height of a person's fame or it destroying the person's fame.<br /> <br /> * A lot of &quot;dead at 28&quot; rock and rollers as well as memorable actors in my setting were Embraced by Toreador and HATE it.<b> Ash</b> from Bloodlines is a perfect example of this being basically River Phoenix.<br /> <br /> * <b>Bela Lugosi </b>IS a vampire but he's an old man who looks nothing like his classic self and bitterly resents his condition.<br /> <br /> * <b>Ed Wood</b> was able to make movies because, well, him being a vampire is the least weird part of his life.<br /> <br /> * I mentioned <b>Al Capone</b> as a vampire is not going to be his classic self but a guy who was severely run down by syphilis and life. Also, he frankly wishes he'd moved to Florida instead of staying in Chicago.<br /> <br /> * In Sookie Stackhouse's books, <b>Elvis </b>(called &quot;Bubba&quot;) is barely intelligent and took to the Embrace poorly because he was half-dead and brain damaged from the pills when the vampire EMT turned him. The other vampires treat him like a pet and he's able to pass himself off as an impersonator or just another redneck with a fetish because he was &quot;Fat Elvis&quot; at best.<br /> <br /> A couple of more fictional examples:<br /> <br /> * <b>Alan Sovereign</b> is actually akin to Bernie Madoff or Jordan Belfort for famous financiers who went crooked. The fact that he served a decade for financial crimes also shows that SOMEONE threw him under the bus and his crimes were especially egregious. I wouldn't be surprised if he actually was a beneficiary of either's malfeasance.<br /> <br /> * Enron just flat out WAS <b>Endron Oil </b>in my setting and Endron Oil actually went bankrupt due to Glass Walker activity. It's been replaced with other companies but hit Pentex hard.<br /> <br /> * <b>Maldavis </b>was actually quite famous as a Chicago Civil Rights leader and was on a bunch of magazine covers due to being so photogenic. It's something that bothers her now that it's 40 years later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-24-2020, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T22:49:57-07:00","id":1415266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1415260#post1415260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While there was a lot of pushback in Revised books against the idea of &quot;George Washington was a vampire,&quot; and rightly so (early books could be a little gonzo about it), more obscure historical figures make great vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than use historical figures, if I want them to be a supernatural creature than I replace the real world person with a fictional one, and then embrace that person. It's like how James Clavell created &quot;Toranaga&quot; in Shogun to replace Tokugawa Ieyasu, or that &quot;Dirk Struan&quot; was a veiled William Jardine in Tai-Pan or that &quot;Struan &amp; Company&quot; is Jardine Matheson &amp; Company. In fact, I love Clavell's Asian Saga so much, I actually use these fictional characters in my own chronicles history. I call this the &quot;Johnny Fontaine Rule&quot; since the Godfather novels and movies famously used the fictional Johnny Fontaine as a roman-a-clef of Frank Sinatra.<br /> <br /> When I ran a vampire chronicle in Chicago (which used the details on Ballard I posted above), I used &quot;Sal Ciccone&quot; as my Al Capone stand-in precisely because 1) I anticipated the PCs might do something to him and felt more comfortable using a fictional character that deviated from history than the real person, and 2) if things went as planned, Sal Ciccone would be embraced by Lodin like he did in the canonical history with Capone.<br /> <br /> I think that respects the historical person while acknowledging how awesome it can be as an inspiration.<br /> <br /> I do make exceptions as there is <i>no way</i> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vseslav_of_Polotsk\" target=\"_blank\">Vselav of Polotsk</a> is <i>not</i> a Silver Fang king of the Garou. The older and more obscure the historical figure is, the more I would be willing to make them supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1415260#post1415260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, with wraiths, you can go all out. I recall a thread in which a poster had Julius Caesar be the Smiling Lord, which I liked. Why not, when you have Bismarck as the anacreon of Berlin and Qin Shi Huang as the ruler of Yellow Springs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was me because that's true in my chronicles, and I know I posted that in the Wraith forum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T23:00:21-07:00","id":1415267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1415197#post1415197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is great and exactly the kind of thing I was think of. It gives some character to the WoD, more so than just being &quot;our world with vampires.&quot; It also would give an odd quality to any vampire who knows history meeting Ballard, as he is a historical figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely gave that NPC more gravitas in the chronicle. When a PC finally met him, and I then explained how his character already knew of Ballard from mortal history, and that he recognized him as being the same figure, the PC certainly acted very differently than he was planning. Just knowing this vampire had vast &quot;historical&quot; achievements as a mortal would cause the PCs to tread more cautiously around him.<br /> <br /> I have to admit that Ballard is my favorite character in the Chicago chronicles because he's such a magnificent piece of shit. He's capable and powerful, but has real weaknesses. So he's a great antagonist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T07:51:35-07:00","id":1415296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1415262#post1415262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Enron just flat out WAS <b>Endron Oil </b>in my setting and Endron Oil actually went bankrupt due to Glass Walker activity. It's been replaced with other companies but hit Pentex hard.<br /> <br /> * <b>Maldavis </b>was actually quite famous as a Chicago Civil Rights leader and was on a bunch of magazine covers due to being so photogenic. It's something that bothers her now that it's 40 years later.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is my take on Enron/ Endron as well, though I've got Virtual Adepts thrown in as well. And that's a good take on Maldavis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T10:25:16-07:00","id":1484116,"title":"","content":"I would use 3 persons famous in real world:<br /> <br /> Hugh Williams - the unsinkable Wraith from Menai strait. At least 3 ships sunk there on the same date (5th of December) and there was only one survivor, always named Hugh Williams. Some source states that this is only a legend but what if it's true?<br /> <br /> Wojtek - a syrian brown bear adopted by polish soldiers during II WW. I would make him a Gurahl still living today (he faked his death as an hibernation trance). <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wojtek_(bear\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wojtek_(bear</a>)<br /> <br /> Hercules - another Gurahl, this time a wrestler and actor.<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hercules_(bear\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hercules_(bear</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T18:24:18-07:00","id":1484252,"title":"","content":"I lament that there was never a classic sourcebook about the Fame background and how to work with it in chronicles, including characters who were famous while alive and what happens after the embrace, and vampires who become famous and how the Masquerade deals with that.<br /> <br /> As for famous-in-life vampires, I like to imagine that 90s blues guitarist turned Ravnos Brian Thompson has turned into a sort of blues version of Elvis, with fans debating if he is still alive or not and his original CDs going for large sums on the collectors' market. Meanwhile, people swear they've seen someone who looks and sounds just like him but is too young to be a man of 50 at various small bars and clubs, with bad luck and trouble always following in his wake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T18:47:36-07:00","id":1484253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1484252#post1484252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for famous-in-life vampires, I like to imagine that 90s blues guitarist turned Ravnos Brian Thompson has turned into a sort of blues version of Elvis, with fans debating if he is still alive or not and his original CDs going for large sums on the collectors' market. Meanwhile, people swear they've seen someone who looks and sounds just like him but is too young to be a man of 50 at various small bars and clubs, with bad luck and trouble always following in his wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Brian Thompson, the <a href=\"https://aminoapps.com/c/horror/page/blog/brian-thompson-appreciation-post/5BZF_VuPbd1Q1brGdYe7Gd3lYQdbXm7\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Actor</i></a>? He was the bad guy in <b>so</b> many things in the 80s and 90s, he was the bad guy in Kindred; the Embrace! Imagine coming out of a Brian Thompson movie marathon, going outside for some air, and seeing him climbing up the wall of the apartment building next door?<br /> <br /> Of course, the real Brian Thompson is still alive and doing well, so his life may have had to take a darker turn in the WoD...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 06-16-2022, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T05:05:27-07:00","id":1484283,"title":"","content":"I think in the end the idea of coming up with fictional famous people and attributing fictional fame to already existing characters works better than making real life people into supernaturals. It gives more freedom do adapt the character and less expectations on how they should be and behave and what should be true about them.<br /> <br /> This is specially important when you want to link mundane events with supernatural ones. As a rule of thumb, if someone from real life is supposed to exist or have existed in the WoD, they should do so in the same way and have no confirmed supernatural link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T09:24:37-07:00","id":1484363,"title":"","content":"I like this idea of having some npcs or even your own characters having some degree of fame in pop culture and some of the downsides to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T07:12:53-07:00","id":1494136,"title":"","content":"Just as a bit amusement, I decided there was a Disney animated movie about the folklore, or legend, of Lucita.<br /> <br /> It is one of the Disney Princesses movies, and one of the last of the classical era. Say, one that involved Don Bluth. It features her as the first, and neglected, child of the king who is turned over to a priest because she is such a problem child. But the priest is secretly wicked, but lucky for her a prince is around to help save her. In the end she and the prince escape. But along the way there are a lot of the standard tropes from a Disney Princess movie; the princess singing a song about what she wants out of life, a villain song which might be the best in the picture, some animal friends, a fight scene at the end, and so on.<br /> <br /> The Lucita princess costumes, toys and so on are part of the usually stuff Disney sells. The movie got a couple of straight to DVD sequels in the 1990s. A live action remake is due in a few years.<br /> <br /> Christopher Houghton arranged the movie to spite Lucita after she turned him down at some point. Her friends, and basically anyone who has met her, know better than to bring the movie up in conversation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-02-2022, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T13:21:53-07:00","id":1494150,"title":"","content":"How about Ben \u201cBugusy\u201d Segel as a ghoul for The Hecate and they used a version of him in Matthew Forbeck Vegas Knights novel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T15:05:21-07:00","id":1494158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1494136#post1494136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a bit amusement, I decided there was a Disney animated movie about the folklore, or legend, of Lucita.<br /> <br /> It is one of the Disney Princesses movies, and one of the last of the classical era. Say, one that involved Don Bluth. It features her as the first, and neglected, child of the king who is turned over to a priest because she is such a problem child. But the priest is secretly wicked, but lucky for her a prince is around to help save her. In the end she and the prince escape. But along the way there are a lot of the standard tropes from a Disney Princess movie; the princess singing a song about what she wants out of life, a villain song which might be the best in the picture, some animal friends, a fight scene at the end, and so on.<br /> <br /> The Lucita princess costumes, toys and so on are part of the usually stuff Disney sells. The movie got a couple of straight to DVD sequels in the 1990s. A live action remake is due in a few years.<br /> <br /> Christopher Houghton arranged the movie to spite Lucita after she turned him down at some point. Her friends, and basically anyone who has met her, know better than to bring the movie up in conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must admit that is probably the first time <b>ever</b> something to do with Christopher Houghton entertained me.<br /> <br /> I do have in mind to add the idea of a Disney Princess movie related to Lucita's folk legend in my table, though the actual history might probably be closer to Brave, as i previously mentioned. Incidentally the Disney interpretation of her was also adapted into a Soul Edge character about the same time as Darth Vader.<br /> <br /> Extra hilarity in that Fatima Al-Faqadi had already been a Soul Edge &amp; Assassin's Creed and other action games regular for decades, thanks to the shenanigans of the Legacy (of Caine), a cabal of anarch-noddists that happen to have control of a major game studio. To the point of a number of younger Assamites, Ashirra and neonates of a number of arab-speaking or islamic countries being utterly amazed to shocked by the discovery that she actually exists.<br /> <br /> Same for a number of neonates really into videogames in life or unlife. Fatima is overall confused and <b><i>quite</i></b> annoyed by her sudden fame, not to mention tongue-in-cheek comments by those ancillae or <i>silsila </i>aware of it, in the last decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-02-2022, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T16:50:58-07:00","id":1494162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1415260#post1415260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond vampires, mages can make even better famous people. I recall some pretty recent Mage material having Queen Victoria be a Technocrat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Queen Victoria was never Awakened, much less a Technocrat. If she was, there would be good odds that she would still be alive and around at least within the Union. Merely she and her husband, Prince Albert, were strong supporters of the Order of Reason and major players in it's reorganization into the Technocracy. That said, they were probably both Extraordinary Citizens (the Technocrat version of Sorcerers and Acolytes).<br /> <br /> Also it wasn't new information. The Victorian Reorganization and Queen Victoria's involvement in it dates at least as far back as 2E.<br /> <br /> That said, Queen Victoria being a Luminary and later Technocrat could make for some interesting stories, both within the Victorian Era and beyond it as like I said, odds would be pretty good that she would alive into today if she were Awakened. Obviously she would have to end her reign as Queen eventually, her death being faked and focusing full time on the Technocracy. In fact she would be young enough that Paradox may not have forced her off Earth by the time of the Avatar Storm, potentially making her one of the oldest Technocrats on Earth and one with a lot of influence in the post-Avatar Storm world. In fact I could see her easily becoming the defacto leader of the Union post-Avatar Storm in such a scenario. Whether that would be a good or bad thing is a whole other story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1494136#post1494136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a bit amusement, I decided there was a Disney animated movie about the folklore, or legend, of Lucita.<br /> <br /> It is one of the Disney Princesses movies, and one of the last of the classical era. Say, one that involved Don Bluth. It features her as the first, and neglected, child of the king who is turned over to a priest because she is such a problem child. But the priest is secretly wicked, but lucky for her a prince is around to help save her. In the end she and the prince escape. But along the way there are a lot of the standard tropes from a Disney Princess movie; the princess singing a song about what she wants out of life, a villain song which might be the best in the picture, some animal friends, a fight scene at the end, and so on.<br /> <br /> The Lucita princess costumes, toys and so on are part of the usually stuff Disney sells. The movie got a couple of straight to DVD sequels in the 1990s. A live action remake is due in a few years.<br /> <br /> Christopher Houghton arranged the movie to spite Lucita after she turned him down at some point. Her friends, and basically anyone who has met her, know better than to bring the movie up in conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>For bonus points, the Prince is a thinly veiled male Disney version of Lucita's sometimes lover, Fatima.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T05:54:02-07:00","id":1494206,"title":"","content":"It's canon that El Diablo Verde has merchandising and a fandom that acts as his herd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T08:39:40-07:00","id":1494217,"title":"","content":"Personally, maybe because I came into the game with VtM Revisited and 1ed of Requiem, but I like that famous humans don't become or are supernatural and that vampires were at &quot;best&quot; humans with lots of potential as opposed to established and famous people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T06:31:34-07:00","id":1494454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414694-famous-in-the-wod?p=1494217#post1494217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, maybe because I came into the game with VtM Revisited and 1ed of Requiem, but I like that famous humans don't become or are supernatural and that vampires were at &quot;best&quot; humans with lots of potential as opposed to established and famous people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that's the way it &quot;should be&quot; but I l also note that I think there would be exceptions and these exceptions would be the sort of thing that vampires talk about.<br /> <br /> In Bloodlines, one of the characters is a former actor who was Embraced by his Toreador master because he was dying of a drug overdose and had to immediately retreat from the public limelight. This is something he loathes and he desires to once more be famous but can't because it will get him killed. The character was apparently named for River Phoenix and presumably shows how something like this might have gone in the WOD.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-06-2022, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T20:02:32-07:00","id":1494489,"title":"","content":"In general I think the Toreador are by far the most likely to embrace famous people - actors, musicians, artists, writers, etc, in an attempt to &quot;preserve&quot; their talents. Or even just because the vampire is a fan of the actor or whatever. Other clans generally steer clear of embracing famous people because it's not worth the trouble. The Nosferatu are known for occasionally embracing famous beautiful assholes in order to teach them lessons, but there's little risk of those people being recognized as their old mortal self.<br /> <br /> Still pretty rare overall, but if someone wants to play a famous movie star or pop artist or whatever, it's plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T09:40:49-07:00","id":1494529,"title":"","content":"If I was going to have famous people in the WOD here is my two bits.<br /> <br /> Ben &quot;Bugsy&quot; Seagal as a member of the Ventrue or Hecate clan as there main player in Las Vegas and they faked his death at the hands at the mob with a flesh crafted double and maybe even altered his appearance and blood bonded him to keep him under control.<br /> <br /> Billy The Kid being a Gangrel or Brujah member of the Sabbat and loves watching the movies about his exploits on his down time.<br /> <br /> Bass Reeves who was a dedicated law man and being embraced by the Banu Haqium to bring out of control kindred back in line..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T22:02:53-07:00","id":1520080,"title":"","content":"For my V20 headcanon, I freely roll with the idea of famous figures from history and folklore getting Embraced as well as certain WoD characters being historical figures in their mortal days as well. I've even incorporated quite a few fictional characters from books, movies, video games, and anime into my WoD headcanon as well.<br /> <br /> Btw, I like the idea of Lucita de Aragon being a folklore princess later turned into a Disney Princess. I'm gonna use that for my setting from now on.<br /> <br /> Here's a few of my ideas....<br /> <br /> 1. John Wilkes Booth is a Toreador. He was Embraced while he was on the run from the Union Army after Ford's Theater. The person killed in the tobacco barn by federal troops was just a hapless farmhand misidentified as Booth. His sire gave him the Embrace due to his status as an actor and was unaware of Lincoln's assassination at the time. This sort of dovetails nicely into a lot of the old folklore and urban legends about John Wilkes Booth somehow evading his captors and living to a ripe old age under an assumed identity.<br /> <br /> 2. Speaking of which, Billy The Kid is also a vampire. Specifically a Brujah Anarch living in Albuquerque.<br /> <br /> 3. Carter Stanley is a Toreador Antitribbu based out of West Virginia but he isn't happy about it at all. He's Sabbat in name only and the Vaulderie was weak on him. He mostly just stays out of everyone's way and feeds on wild animals and the occasional sex worker and does a side hustle as a street busker or session musician. The wraith of his mother Lucy Stanley occasionally watches out for him and is trying to get him in contact with the Inconnu so he can achieve the Rebirth or at least Golconda, though he is currently unaware of this.<br /> <br /> 4. This one is Mage-related but it ties into the West Virginia setting mentioned earlier. Homer Hickam is a high-ranking member of the Void Engineers and is a Technocratic insider operating within NASA. However, he is very old despite his high levels of Enlightened Science and has recently been sent by the Union back to his boyhood home of Coalwood, West Virginia for one last mission. However, he has a small squad of younger Void Engineer operatives to back him up.<br /> <br /> 5. Ryuta, Kazu, and Hikari (originally from the web animation &quot;<i>Star Love Zero Gravity</i>&quot; by the artist Maruten) are younger Void Engineers who are physically fit and have a decent enough grasp of Enlightened Science but they are also a lot more inexperienced on the street level and have spent a disproportionate amount of time in the Deep Umbra aboard their vessel, the CS Exeter. The Technocratic Union has called them away from their Deep Umbral duties to instead back up Homer Hickam in West Virginia to investigate a very terrifying and powerful spiritual anomaly that could give the likes of both Metathiax and Kupala a run for their money.<br /> <br /> 6. Strahd Von Zarovich is the Archbishop of West Virginia. He is a member of Old Clan Tzimisce but he threw his lot in with the Sabbat unlike most of the Old Clan. Strahd was closely allied with members of the Cappadocian Clan and was able to learn Necromancy in the Dark Medieval era, which makes him a very crucial asset for the Sabbat. Due to some unfortunate disputes with some of the Lasombra elders in Mexico City during the early 19th Century, he was never given the chance to become Archbishop of a place like Detroit or Montreal but instead the relative backwater of West Virginia. His haven is in the capital city of Charleston but the domain extends across the entire state, used by the Sabbat's nomads as a way station whenever trying to launch raids on places like Pittsburgh, Washington DC, Youngstown, Dayton, Richmond, Greensboro, or Charlotte. Zarovich's diocese is one of very low prestige but of relatively high importance to the Sword of Caine.<br /> <br /> 7. Roy DeMeo is a Malkavian Antitribbu currently exiled from NYC and is Ductus of a nomadic pack.<br /> <br /> 8. Cuthbert Beckett was a noted historian and polymath even prior to his Embrace and excerpts from his various treatises and almanacs from his mortal days are often required reading in high schools and colleges.<br /> <br /> 9. Maximilian Strauss was a sorcerer and occultist prior to Embrace. He's not as well-known as someone like John Dee or Edward Kelley, but you can occasionally find some of his translated writings for sale in specialty occult bookstores.<br /> <br /> 10. Ming Xiao was a very influential princess in the later Han Dynasty's decadent imperial courts prior to her Embrace by a Toreador elder and she may have been the fabled Diaochan mentioned in The Romance of The Three Kingdoms. She eventually became a leader within the Quincunx Court and was the Ancestor of Luoyang for many years. But when the majority of East Asian Cainite courts pledged nominal loyalty to the Camarilla, she saw this as unforgivable. Even if the Eastern courts were largely de facto independent, she still viewed it as bowing to the Western Cainites. Eventually, she cliqued up with the Sabbat in the late 1800's and learned the Discipline of Vicissitude through a mix of Vaulderie and diablerizing convicted infernalists. She eventually joined forces with the Tzimisce elder Andrei and waged a crusade to take Los Angeles in 2004. This ended very badly and it is presumed she met Final Death in 2004 alongside Andrei and several other Kindred.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!",